    <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=\sin{x}</m>, and let <m>k</m> be a real number. Let <m>F(x)=f(x^k)</m> and <m>G(x)=[f(x)]^k</m>.</p>
<p>Find expressions for (a) <m>F'(x)</m> and (b) <m>G'(x)</m>.</p>
<p>(a) <m>F'(x)=</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) <m>G'(x)=</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\cos\mathopen{}\left(x^{k}\right)kx^{k-1}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>k\mathopen{}\left(\sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\right)^{k-1}\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
